# sprint_sec_sh.oot — SEC hostile audit of sh.oo / planned sh_arg_ok
# Date: 2026-08-13
# Role: SEC. This file only. No product edit. Did not touch sh.oo.
# Marker: pre-DE1 snapshot
# Surfaces: ooda/std/sh.oo (164 L), ooda/std/os/process.oo,
#           ooda/runtime/chs_rt_sys.c, ooda/std/os/env.oo,
#           openOODA/CAPS.oot, openOODA/audit/foundation_rollup.oot DE10
# Method: re-read sh.oo after HYG reported sh_arg.oo absent; static hunt
#         of sinks, EnvCap vs TMPDIR, and what a char-class gate still
#         cannot seal. No live inject probe this turn. Do not claim secure.
## VERDICT
DE1 **did not land**. `sh_arg_ok` is not in `ooda/std/sh.oo`.
`ooda/std/sh_arg.oo` is absent. `ooda/scripts/sh_arg_ok_smoke.oo` is absent.
Every interpolated argument still goes raw into `process_exec` →
`sys_exec(p, "sh", "-c", shell_cmd)`.

19 of 20 functions are Critical shell-injection sinks. Only `sh_sleep`
takes an `Int`. DE10 said this. The tree has not moved.

A future char-class gate is not a seal. git / tar / chmod stay shell
even after it. ProcessCap still reads env. Do not green this wave.

---
DE1 STATUS — pre-DE1 snapshot
---

Re-read `/home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda/std/sh.oo` this turn.

| Probe | Result |
|-------|--------|
| `sh_arg_ok` in sh.oo | **ABSENT** |
| `std/sh_arg.oo` | **ABSENT** (HYG same wave) |
| `requires` beyond `chars_len > 0` | **none** |
| quoting / `--` / argv | **none** |
| residual comment L15 | "shell-string interpolation is the caller's job; no argv facade" |

`process_exec` (`ooda/std/os/process.oo:34-38`) is `sys_exec(p, "sh", "-c", shell_cmd)`.
Runtime `oo_sys_exec` (`chs_rt_sys.c:224`) is fork+execvp with a filtered
child env and pinned `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin`. That stops parent `IFS` /
`LD_PRELOAD` / attacker `PATH`. It does **not** parse or quote `shell_cmd`.

`chars_len > 0` is not a gate. `"; id"` has length 4.

