REMAINING SINKS (live, no gate)
---

Concat form is `process_exec(p, "CMD " + user)` with no quotes.

| Fn | Line | Concat | Why Critical |
|----|-----:|--------|--------------|
| sh_clean | 24 | `rm -rf ` + dir | `;`, newline, `/*`, leading `-` |
| sh_mkdir_p | 32 | `mkdir -p ` + dir | same |
| sh_copy | 41 | `cp -r ` + src + dst | two unsanitized fields |
| sh_chmod | 50 | `chmod ` + mode + path | mode is flags; `+x` / `-R` / `4755` |
| sh_git_clone | 59 | `git clone ` + url + dst | URL flags, hooks, protocols |
| sh_tar_extract | 68 | `tar -xzf ` + arc + ` -C ` + dst | slip + `--checkpoint-action` |
| sh_chmod_recursive | 77 | `find ` + path + ` -exec chmod ` + mode + ` {} +` | find extra predicates |
| sh_curl_get | 95 | `curl -s ` + url | `--output`, file://, SSRF |
| sh_which | 101 | `command -v ` + name | `;`, glob |
| sh_env_get | 107 | `printenv ` + key | ProcessCap env read; key inject |
| sh_env_get_or | 113 | `printenv ` + key + ` \|\| echo ` + default | key **and** default inject |
| sh_md5sum | 119 | `md5sum ` + path | `;`, `--` |
| sh_sha256sum | 125 | same | same |
| sh_diff | 132 | `diff ` + a + b | two fields |
| sh_grep | 139 | `grep ` + pat + path | pat is a second language |
| sh_basename | 145 | `basename ` + path | |
| sh_dirname | 151 | `dirname ` + path | |
| sh_realpath | 157 | `realpath ` + path | |
| sh_tempfile | 163 | `mktemp ` + template | callers already pass `-d` `-t` |
| sh_sleep | 85 | `sleep ` + Int | **not** a string sink |

Proof of shape (no escape):

    let r = process_exec(p, "rm -rf " + dir);                 # sh.oo:24
    let r = process_exec(p, "git clone " + url + " " + dst);  # sh.oo:59
    let r = process_exec(p, "find " + path + " -exec chmod " + mode + " {} +");
    return process_exec(p, "printenv " + key + " || echo " + default);

Callers that already feed flag soup (so a tight class will break them,
and a loose class will keep the hole):

- `sh_tempfile(p, "-d " + tmpd + " -t ecap_XXXXXX")` — ecap/ehitl/etc/fs_writedir smokes
- `sh_chmod(p, "+x", root + "/scripts/ooda_apply_fix.oo")` — ooda_apply_ecap_fix.oo:27

`sh_git_clone` / `sh_tar_extract` / `sh_chmod_recursive` have **no**
script callers yet. They are still exported product API.

Adjacent (not sh.oo, still sh -c): `cmd_execute` arity >5 joins with
spaces (`ooda/std/os/cmd.oo:54-61`). `scenario.oo` exec helpers.
`shell_safety_smoke.oo` does **not** test sh.oo interpolation; it
pokes product `check` with quoted env. That smoke is not this seal.

---
CHAR-CLASS GATE — bypass list (what still injects)
---

DE1 is expected to fail-closed on a character class. No implementation
to attack. Below is the class of holes that survive **any** typical
gate on this concat design. Blacklist of `$ ; | & \` ' "` is weaker
than ASCII whitelist `[A-Za-z0-9._/-]`. Scripts will force the weak
one: `+x`, `-d`, `-t`, `https://`, and spaces are already in callers.

| Vector | Blacklist (`$` / &#124; / `&`) | Tight ASCII whitelist | Still injects after tight whitelist? |
|--------|----------------------|------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| newline `\n` | **INJECT** (`rm -rf x\nid`) | deny | no (must deny CR/LF/NEL/U+2028/U+2029) |
| `\r` / `\r\n` | display lie; `\n` injects | deny if not listed | no if rejected |
| IFS from **parent** env | DE1.8 drops IFS | n/a | **no** — child IFS is default. Not a sh.oo win |
| `IFS=` **inside the string** | needs `=` and space in command position | deny `=` / space | no on tight class; **yes** if space allowed |
| glob `*` `?` `[` | `rm -rf /*` | deny `*` `?` `[` | no if denied; **yes** if `*` kept for paths |
| env `printenv KEY` | key `; id` injects | deny metachar | command inject no; **OODA_* leak remains** |
| env `echo DEFAULT` | `; id` / `` `id` `` | deny | no on tight class |
| `--` / leading `-` | `chmod -R /`, `git clone --upload-pack=…`, `curl --output`, `tar --checkpoint-action=exec=` | **INJECT** if `-` allowed | **YES** — class does not restore `--` |
| path starts with `-` | `sh_clean("-rf /")` → `rm -rf -rf /` | `-` usually allowed | **YES** |
| unicode homoglyphs (`＄` `；` fullwidth) | pass blacklist; POSIX sh does not treat them as meta | deny (non-ASCII) | usually **no** on POSIX sh; do not call this a unicode seal without a probe |
| overlong / NUL | C string cuts at NUL; length-based concat can hide a tail | walk must use byte length, then refuse NUL | truncation, not extra command, if `.data` is C |
| `../` and `/` | not meta | allowed | **YES** — `sh_clean("/")`, `sh_clean("../../")` |
| find predicate | `path = ". -o -exec id {} +"` | needs space and `-` | **YES** if those stay (callers need them) |
| grep pat | regex + flags | alnum-only pats | **YES** if `.` `*` stay |
| git URL | `:` `/` | URL class | **YES** — any host; hooks run in the clone |
| tar members | n/a | n/a | **YES** — path slip is archive content, not argv class |
| chmod mode | `4755`, `u+s`, `-R` | `+` needed for `+x` | **YES** — setuid / recursive stay representable |

What a landed `sh_arg_ok` **can** stop, if it is a fail-closed
whitelist that includes newline and the classic meta set:
`;` `|` `&` `` ` `` `$` `(` `)` `<` `>` newline quote backslash.

What it **cannot** stop: option injection, path traversal, glob if
`*` lives, find `-exec` rewriting, tar slip, git hook/protocol RCE,
chmod mode semantics, curl/file SSRF, ProcessCap `printenv` of
`OODA_*` / `OO_*` / `PATH`.

If DE1 allows space + `-` so `sh_tempfile("-d " + tmpd + " -t …")`
keeps compiling, treat option injection and find-injection as **open**.

---
SIGNATURE FREEZE — ProcessCap + TMPDIR (correct, and a lie)
---

Do **not** change `sh_env_get` / `sh_env_get_or` to take `&EnvCap`.

Proof:

1. SCRIPTING.oot lets `main(p: &ProcessCap)` exist with no EnvCap.
2. Dozens of scripts only have ProcessCap and call
   `sh_env_get_or(p, "TMPDIR", ".ooda-cache/ooda-tmp")` (and
   `OODAC_BIN`, `OODA`, `OODA_BIN`, `WASMTIME`, `EMIT_TIMEOUT`).
3. `env_get` (`ooda/std/os/env.oo`) needs `&EnvCap` and
   `oo_process_policy_getenv` (`chs_rt_sys.c:121-126`) returns NULL
   unless the key starts with `OODA_` or `OO_`.
4. `TMPDIR` is neither. EnvCap would **deny**. Freeze is correct.

Honesty on the same path (not a reason to add EnvCap):

- Child exec env keeps only `OODA_*` / `OO_*` plus pinned PATH.
  `printenv TMPDIR` in that child **always fails**. Scripts always
  hit `echo DEFAULT`. They do not read host TMPDIR today.
- `OODAC_BIN` is not `OODA_` (5th byte is `C`, not `_`). Same miss.
- `OODA` (4 chars) is not `OODA_` and not `OO_`. Same miss.
- `OODA_BIN` **is** `OODA_`. Child inherits it. `printenv OODA_BIN`
  is a ProcessCap env read of a policy key. EnvCap never entered.
  wasm_execute / wasm_emit / max_cycles_recursion use this key.
- Any other `OODA_*` / `OO_*` (writedir, FFI allow, HITL, secrets
  someone prefixed) is readable the same way. ProcessCap is a
  second, wider env API. CAPS.oot says EnvCap is the env token.
  sh.oo ignores that.

Further honesty: `oo_sys_exec` success value is `oo_str_lit("")`
(`chs_rt_sys.c:289-291`). No stdout capture. Even `printenv OODA_BIN`
does not return the value through `Result`. `sh_*` "read ops" are
exit-status wrappers. A char-class gate does not fix that.

---
git / tar / chmod STAY SHELL AFTER A GATE
---

DE10 (foundation_rollup.oot) already ordered:

- chmod / mkdir / copy / clean / tempfile → native `fs_*` + FsWriteCap
- git clone / tar extract → `DangerShellCap` (name **not** in CAPS.oot)
- env → `oo_env_get` + EnvCap (blocked for TMPDIR; see freeze)

None of that is this wave. After `sh_arg_ok`:

| Op | Still | Residual that a class cannot close |
|----|-------|-------------------------------------|
| sh_git_clone | `sh -c "git clone " + url + " " + dst` | `--upload-pack`, `-c core.fsmonitor`, `ext::`, post-checkout hooks |
| sh_tar_extract | `sh -c "tar -xzf " + arc + " -C " + dst` | member `../`, `--checkpoint-action=exec=`, symlink escape |
| sh_chmod | `sh -c "chmod " + mode + " " + path` | `-R`, `u+s`, `4755` on a caller path |
| sh_chmod_recursive | `find PATH -exec chmod MODE {} +` | extra find expr; mode as above |

`std/os/cmd.oo` already has argv `sys_exec` up to 5 args. sh.oo does
not use it. The gate keeps the shell. That is the residual.

CAPS.oot has ProcessCap for exec and EnvCap for env. No DangerShellCap.
No FsWriteCap on any sh_* mutate. ProcessCap is the whole OS.

---
RESIDUAL (do not close on paper)
---

- **DE1 not landed.** pre-DE1 snapshot. 19 concat sinks live.
- Char-class, when it lands, is a meta filter. Not argv. Not a cap.
- Signature freeze for `sh_env_get_or(&ProcessCap, key, default)` is
  **correct**. EnvCap would deny TMPDIR. The TMPDIR read is already
  dead in the child. The OODA_* read is a real EnvCap bypass.
- git / tar / chmod / find -exec remain shell + tool RCE after any
  class. Native fs_* / argv / a real DangerShellCap are not here.
- `oo_sys_exec` returns empty Ok. sh_* reads do not return stdout.
- No inject/refuse proof this turn (no gate to fail). When DE1
  lands, refuse: newline, `;`, `$(`, leading `-`, `*`, find `-o`,
  `git --upload-pack`, `tar --checkpoint-action`, `printenv OODA_`.
  Do not PASS on "alnum looks fine."

**Not secure.** Not path-A. Same DE10 hole plus a planned class that
cannot eat git/tar/chmod.
